    "https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18349": {
      "title": "Parking Enforcement Attendant, part-time",
      "description": "Careers at Bowdoin College | Parking Enforcement Attendant, part-time Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Parking Enforcement Attendant, part-time Bookmark this Job Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If selected as a finalist, you will be required to submit information for three references, including name, email address, phone number and how you know the reference. Posting Details Posting Details Title Parking Enforcement Attendant, part-time Posting Number C00445JP Department Safety and Security Job Summary The Casual Parking Enforcement Attendant provides measured enforcement of College parking regulations through the Office of Safety and Security. By following established procedures and employing good common sense, the Parking Enforcement Attendant will work effectively with Safety and Security officers, along with students, faculty, staff, and visitors, contributing to the overall safety of the Campus. Essential Functions: Acquire and maintain a thorough knowledge of the college campus and layout of streets, buildings, and other significant areas of the college campus so as to maximize the accuracy of documentation. Be thoroughly familiar with the Department of Safety and Security’s organizational philosophy. Assist in ensuring good public relations between the College and local communities, and provide general assistance to all persons on the campus including information regarding campus locations, special events, and campus regulations. Identify vehicles in violation of parking regulations, checking with Safety and Security Communications, when necessary, to confirm vehicle and owner information before issuing parking violations or warnings. Relay information to Safety and Security Communications relating to incidents or emergencies, using two-way radios or cell phone. Observe and report hazardous conditions such as malfunctioning traffic signals, missing signs, and the absence of parking and street markings. The hourly rate for this position is $18.40 per hour. Education/Skills Requirements Education/Skills Requirements A high school diploma or GED equivalent. A valid driver’s license and the ability to meet the requirements of the College’s Motor Vehicle Use Policy. Strong interpersonal, verbal, and written communications skills. Capacity to interact calmly with diverse individuals in dynamic and occasionally stressful. situations. Ability to multi-task in a busy fast-paced work environment. Ability to complete detailed written documentation. Ability to work independently, or as part of a team. Regular, reliable, and punctual attendance. Experience Requirements and/or Equivalents No prior experience is required; Some relevant experience preferred Applicants must meet the minimum qualifications in this posting to be considered for hire. Standard Work Days and Hours This is an onsite, part-time, non-benefit eligible position working less than 19 hours/week on Monday to Friday from 11:00 am – 3:00 pm Employment at Bowdoin College is contingent upon satisfactory completion of applicable background checks including but not limited to: criminal records, educational verifications, driving records (when job-related), and/or credit history (when job related). We regret that Bowdoin College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for staff positions. #bcindeed About Bowdoin Bowdoin embraces diversity in all forms, and the College is home to talented students, faculty and staff—with a variety of racial, ethnic, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds; religious beliefs; and gender identities, among other factors. We encourage applications from candidates committed to the support of an inclusive campus community and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. We value a community in which individuals of all backgrounds are warmly welcomed and encouraged to succeed. Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Shift N/A Employment Category Casual Benefits Eligible No Pay Type Hourly Background Check Package Requirements Support Staff + MVR Is driving a vehicle (e.g. Bowdoin vehicle or off road vehicle, rental car, personal car) an essential function of this job? Yes Is a pre-placement physical required for this position? No Posting Date 09/04/2026 Applications Accepted Until Open Until Filled No Type of Posting Internal/External Special Instructions to Applicants If selected as a finalist, you will be required to submit information for three references, including name, email address, phone number and how you know the reference. EEO Information Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Indeed.com Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Ed Facebook Glassdoor Google Search HigherEdJobs.com InsideHigherEd.com LinkedIn Twitter MANP Maine Job Link LiveandWorkinMaine.com Employee Referral Bowdoin College Website Radio Ad TechMaine NCAA CASE Other If you answered Employee Referral or Other, please  specify here: (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Confidential arrangements will be made if you have a disability or require an accommodation in completing the application or in the interview process. Please notify Human Resources at (207) 725-3837 in advance so all necessary arrangements can be made confidentially. Staff & Casual contact: careers@bowdoin.edu Faculty contact: facultycareers@bowdoin.edu (t)207-725-3837 216 Maine Street, Brunswick, ME 04011 Bowdoin College is a member of the Diversity Hiring Coalition of Maine , and Live and Work in Maine . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18108": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Earth and Oceanographic Science",
      "description": "Careers at Bowdoin College | Assistant Professor of Earth and Oceanographic Science Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Assistant Professor of Earth and Oceanographic Science Bookmark this Job Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. At the time of application, you will be required to include information for three references, including name, title, email address, phone number and how you know the reference. Reference providers will receive an automatically-generated email from the application system if the application reaches a certain stage during the review process. The email will provide them a link to upload a confidential reference letter on your behalf. You will not be able to view the reference letters but will be able to see how many have been submitted on your behalf . Posting Details Posting Details Title Assistant Professor of Earth and Oceanographic Science Posting Number F00307JP Department Earth and Oceanographic Science Position Summary Bowdoin College’s Department of Earth and Oceanographic Science invites applications for a full-time tenure-track faculty appointment in geoscience applications of artificial intelligence at the Assistant Professor level, beginning July 1, 2027. We seek candidates whose scholarship critically examines, thoughtfully utilizes, or ethically guides AI to advance understanding of geoscience processes. Areas of geoscience expertise might include glacial geology/geomorphology, glaciology, geophysics, neotectonics, sedimentology, stratigraphy, tectonic geomorphology, or atmospheric science, with a preference for those whose work intersects with surface earth processes and focuses on thousand- to million-year timescales. These fields and timescales have critical intersections with and implications for how humans live on and with Earth, even as the landscape and climate change in response to both natural and human activities. These areas of geoscience expertise also align with the EOS Department’s earth system science approach to investigating fundamental questions about Earth’s past, present, and future. The successful candidate will teach three courses per year, including two courses with separate lab sections. Bowdoin is particularly interested in candidates dedicated to undergraduate teaching and with a promise of long-term, successful scholarship and who will offer opportunities to engage students in research. A Ph.D. in geoscience or a related field is expected by the date of the appointment. Bowdoin’s Hastings Initiative for AI and Humanity aims to critically examine, thoughtfully utilize, and ethically guide AI’s trajectory. A $50 million dollar gift by Reed Hastings funds ten new faculty positions, including this one, across disciplines; supports faculty in AI-related teaching, research, and creative work; sponsors workshops, symposia, and student research; and prepares the next generation of leaders to engage responsibly with the opportunities and challenges presented by artificial intelligence. The College’s location along the rocky Maine coast provides excellent local field sites for teaching and research. Bowdoin maintains a High Performance Computer ( HPC ) cluster and access to GIS software. Department facilities include mineral, rock, and fossil collections; augmented reality sandbox; stream table; rock saws; shallow water current meters; remote water samplers for river analysis; ACDP ; petrographic microscopes; and SEM (Scanning Electron Microscope) with CL/ EDS / EBSD capabilities. For more information, please visit https://www.bowdoin.edu/earth-oceanographicscience/ . Bowdoin College offers opportunities for professional development, a fully-funded, year-long pre-tenure sabbatical leave (after three years of teaching and successful reappointment), and regular, generously funded, post-tenure sabbaticals. Support for teaching, grant submission, computing software, and community partnerships in courses is available. The College also offers robust programming and resources for establishing and enhancing mentoring networks. At Bowdoin, we are committed to inclusive excellence, an ongoing collective practice that honors our institutional commitment to provide an outstanding liberal arts education and serve the common good. The College is home to talented students, faculty and staff and we encourage applications from candidates committed to the inclusive instruction and support of a diverse student population, and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. Accessibility during the application and interview stages, as well as once employed, is a priority of the College: https://www.bowdoin.edu/accessibility/index.html . In addition, visa sponsorships for faculty hires are available. Bowdoin College accepts only electronic submissions. Pleasesubmit the following: (1) a one-page cover letter; (2) a curriculum vitae; (3) a three-page statement that describes your teaching practices, including a description of courses you would be interested in teaching that would enrich existing curriculum in EOS ( https://bowdoin-public.courseleaf.com/courses/eos/ ); (4) a two-page research statement; (5) a one-page statement that describes your philosophy and use of AI; and (6) the names and contact information for three references who have agreed to provide letters of recommendation. Letters will be automatically requested from the references for candidates invited for interviews. Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled. The anticipated hiring range for this appointment at the assistant professor rank without prior tenure-track experience is $92,000 – $98,000 annually; the salary offered will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s experience and with internal peer equity. All offers of employment are contingent upon the successful completion of a satisfactory background check. Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. For further information about the College and our department, please visit our website: http://www.bowdoin.edu . Posting Date 07/28/2026 Applications Accepted Until Open Until Filled Yes Special Instructions to Applicants At the time of application, you will be required to include information for three references, including name, title, email address, phone number and how you know the reference. Reference providers will receive an automatically-generated email from the application system if the application reaches a certain stage during the review process. The email will provide them a link to upload a confidential reference letter on your behalf. You will not be able to view the reference letters but will be able to see how many have been submitted on your behalf . Employment Category Full Time Year Round Job Start Date 07/01/2027 Job End Date Job Type Faculty Background Check Package Requirements Faculty/Administrative Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Research Interests/Research Plans Teaching Philosophy/Principles Artificial Intelligence Statement Optional Documents Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Indeed.com Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Ed Facebook Glassdoor Google Search HigherEdJobs.com InsideHigherEd.com LinkedIn Twitter MANP Maine Job Link LiveandWorkinMaine.com Employee Referral Bowdoin College Website Radio Ad TechMaine NCAA CASE Other If you answered Employee Referral or Other, please  specify here: (Open Ended Question) Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Confidential arrangements will be made if you have a disability or require an accommodation in completing the application or in the interview process. Please notify Human Resources at (207) 725-3837 in advance so all necessary arrangements can be made confidentially. Staff & Casual contact: careers@bowdoin.edu Faculty contact: facultycareers@bowdoin.edu (t)207-725-3837 216 Maine Street, Brunswick, ME 04011 Bowdoin College is a member of the Diversity Hiring Coalition of Maine , and Live and Work in Maine . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
