    "https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18348": {
      "title": "Food Service Worker (late night shift, part-time)",
      "description": "Careers at Bowdoin College | Food Service Worker (late night shift, part-time) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Food Service Worker (late night shift, part-time) Bookmark this Job Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. If selected as a finalist, you will be required to submit information for three references, including name, email address, phone number and how you know the reference. Posting Details Posting Details Title Food Service Worker (late night shift, part-time) Posting Number C00444JP Department Dining Service - Thorne Hall Job Summary Located in Brunswick, Maine, Bowdoin College boasts a student population of almost 2000. Our Dining Services Department makes everything from scratch and are consistently rated in the top 10 for college dining! We have our own butcher shop, bakeshop, and organic garden that all supply food to our two dining halls and three retail locations. Under supervision of dining supervisors and regular staff, we are seeking a part-time, entry-level Food Service Worker/Dining Assistant to support our SuperSnack operation at Thorne Dining Hall. SuperSnack is a highly popular, late-night dining service for students. Responsibilities include: Assisting with ingredient preparation for use in recipes for both hot and cold food production, being mindful of cross contamination of foods Assisting with servery set-up, service, and replenishment Following appropriate food handling and storage procedures; Serve food while adhering to portion control and serving procedures Assisting in dishwashing tasks including scraping dirty dishes, loading and unloading pot and dish machine, and stacking clean dishware Assisting in sanitation duties including cleaning preparation station and hot line, holding and dispensing equipment, sweeping and mopping kitchen, dining room and service areas, cleaning employee restrooms, wiping walls, tables and chairs, and cleaning all kitchen cooking equipment, refrigerated, frozen and dry storage area, as well as dock area Assisting in daily operations and monitoring the dining hall’s checking systems Assisting in stocking the gluten-free area and organizing the stocking inventory following FICO standards Greeting and assisting dining service patrons Verifying student identification/board eligibility for specific meals and verifying meal counts Providing coverage for the front and back of the house, filling in as needed Compensation: The hourly rate for this position is $19.00 per hour 10% Shift Differential for hours worked from 3:00 pm to 11:00 pm 15% Shift Differential for hours worked from 11:00 pm to 2:00 am Supersnack Premium of an additional $4.00 per hour for hours worked from 10:00 pm to 2:00 am Weekend Differential of an additional $1.00 per hour for hours worked on Saturday and Sunday Education/Skills Requirements High school diploma or GED required Current ServSafe certification or completion of the online food safety course upon hire Strong problem-solving skills Strong customer service skills Strong commitment to dependability and punctuality Ability to understand and practice recycling and sustainability practices Ability to prioritize tasks in a fast-paced environment Ability to follow written and verbal direction Ability to perform simple mathematic equations Ability to work independently and as part of a team Working knowledge of good personal hygiene practices Experience Requirements and/or Equivalents Entry level position, no prior work experience required At least one year of experience in food production and/or ingredient preparation techniques and intermediate knife skills (i.e. chopping, dicing, slicing) highly preferred Applicants must meet the minimum qualifications in this posting to be considered for hire. Standard Work Days and Hours This is an onsite, part-time, non-benefit eligible position working less than 20 hours/week The SuperSnack hours are 10:00 pm to 2:00 am Employment at Bowdoin College is contingent upon satisfactory completion of applicable background checks including but not limited to: criminal records, educational verifications, driving records (when job-related), and/or credit history (when job related). We regret that Bowdoin College is unable to provide visa sponsorship for staff positions. #bcindeed About Bowdoin Bowdoin embraces diversity in all forms, and the College is home to talented students, faculty and staff—with a variety of racial, ethnic, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds; religious beliefs; and gender identities, among other factors. We encourage applications from candidates committed to the support of an inclusive campus community and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. We value a community in which individuals of all backgrounds are warmly welcomed and encouraged to succeed. Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Shift Third Shift Employment Category Casual Benefits Eligible No Pay Type Hourly Background Check Package Requirements Support Staff Is driving a vehicle (e.g. Bowdoin vehicle or off road vehicle, rental car, personal car) an essential function of this job? No Is a pre-placement physical required for this position? Yes Posting Date 09/04/2026 Applications Accepted Until Open Until Filled No Type of Posting Internal/External Special Instructions to Applicants If selected as a finalist, you will be required to submit information for three references, including name, email address, phone number and how you know the reference. EEO Information Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you hear about this position? Indeed.com Chronicle of Higher Education Diverse Issues in Higher Ed Facebook Glassdoor Google Search HigherEdJobs.com InsideHigherEd.com LinkedIn Twitter MANP Maine Job Link LiveandWorkinMaine.com Employee Referral Bowdoin College Website Radio Ad TechMaine NCAA CASE Other If you answered Employee Referral or Other, please  specify here: (Open Ended Question) * What days are you available to work during the week? (list days available) (Open Ended Question) * Are there any days of the week and hours that you are unavailable to work? (Open Ended Question) Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Confidential arrangements will be made if you have a disability or require an accommodation in completing the application or in the interview process. Please notify Human Resources at (207) 725-3837 in advance so all necessary arrangements can be made confidentially. Staff & Casual contact: careers@bowdoin.edu Faculty contact: facultycareers@bowdoin.edu (t)207-725-3837 216 Maine Street, Brunswick, ME 04011 Bowdoin College is a member of the Diversity Hiring Coalition of Maine , and Live and Work in Maine . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
