    "https://careers.bowdoin.edu/postings/18339": {
      "title": "Development Chief of Staff and Executive Director of Campaigns",
      "description": "Careers at Bowdoin College | Development Chief of Staff and Executive Director of Campaigns Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Development Chief of Staff and Executive Director of Campaigns Bookmark this Job Posting Print Preview | This job posting does not accept online applications. Please contact your Human Resource Office for instructions on how to apply. Posting Details Posting Details Title Development Chief of Staff and Executive Director of Campaigns Posting Number S01603JP Department Development Administration Job Summary In partnership with Lindauer, Bowdoin College is seeking a Development Chief of Staff and Executive Director of Campaigns for its extraordinary Development and Alumni Relations team. Reporting to the Senior Vice President for Development and Alumni Relations, this leader will serve as a strategic advisor, operational partner, and connective force for a division of nearly 60 professionals. They will be responsible for leading campaign management for Bowdoin’s upcoming comprehensive campaign as well as future institutional priorities. The successful candidate will bring significant fundraising and campaign experience, strong judgment, and the ability to build trust and create clarity in a complex, fast-moving environment. Bowdoin offers an experienced advancement leader the opportunity to build the structures and partnerships that will turn ambitious institutional priorities into lasting impact. The salary range for this position is $240,000–$260,000 annually. To learn more, apply, or nominate a candidate, please visit: https://lindauerglobal.co/BowdoinChiefOfStaff Education/Skills Requirements Bachelor’s degree required; advanced degree preferred. • Demonstrated ability to manage large teams and complex multi-year projects. • Experience with comprehensive campaigns, including silent phase strategy, case development, and volunteer management. Experience Requirements and/or Equivalents Minimum 10 years of fundraising experience with increasingly significant responsibilities in major gifts, development operations, campaign management, strategic planning, and team leadership, ideally in higher education or a complex nonprofit. Standard Work Days and Hours Standard administrative hours are 8:30am – 5:00pm. Exempt positions require the time commitment necessary to complete the essential duties of the position. About Bowdoin Bowdoin embraces diversity in all forms, and the College is home to talented students, faculty and staff—with a variety of racial, ethnic, cultural, and socioeconomic backgrounds; religious beliefs; and gender identities, among other factors. We encourage applications from candidates committed to the support of an inclusive campus community and those who will enrich and contribute to the College’s multifaceted diversity. We value a community in which individuals of all backgrounds are warmly welcomed and encouraged to succeed. Founded in 1794, Bowdoin has maintained its commitment to the liberal arts for well over 200 years. Bowdoin’s reputation as a preeminent liberal arts college rests on the excellence of its faculty, students, and staff; intimate size; strong sense of community; and connections to the people, history, and natural beauty of Maine. Bowdoin’s campus is situated in a beautiful natural setting. Located in Brunswick, Maine, a town of approximately 20,000, the College is a short drive from the Maine coast, twenty-five miles from Portland and 120 miles from Boston. Shift Employment Category Full Time Year Round FTE 1.00 Benefits Eligible Yes Pay Type Salaried Background Check Package Requirements Faculty/Administrative Is driving a vehicle (e.g. Bowdoin vehicle or off road vehicle, rental car, personal car) an essential function of this job? No Is a pre-placement physical required for this position? No Posting Date 09/04/2026 Applications Accepted Until Open Until Filled No Type of Posting Internal/External Special Instructions to Applicants EEO Information Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Bowdoin College complies with applicable provisions of federal and state laws that prohibit unlawful discrimination in employment, admission, or access to its educational or extracurricular programs, activities, or facilities based on race, color, ethnicity, ancestry and national origin, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity and/or expression, age, marital status, place of birth, genetic predisposition, veteran status, or against qualified individuals with physical or mental disabilities on the basis of disability, or any other legally protected statuses. Confidential arrangements will be made if you have a disability or require an accommodation in completing the application or in the interview process. Please notify Human Resources at (207) 725-3837 in advance so all necessary arrangements can be made confidentially. Staff & Casual contact: careers@bowdoin.edu Faculty contact: facultycareers@bowdoin.edu (t)207-725-3837 216 Maine Street, Brunswick, ME 04011 Bowdoin College is a member of the Diversity Hiring Coalition of Maine , and Live and Work in Maine . To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
